  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban District Council, 15 January 1932; nine nominations for nine seats, so there was no contest (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1932, p. 9). The Northern Whig of the same date states that as the total nominations did not exceed the vacancies there would be no contest, and names the same nine. The retiring councillors who did not seek re-election were Sherrard, Love and Kane. No party label was printed. Returned unopposed."
